# Tests allowed to skip. A skip and a pass print the same word, so every skip
# that fires has to be a reviewed line rather than a silence.
#
# Adding a name here means the guard it carries is knowingly not running.
# Removing a test from this list is required the moment it stops skipping,
# because a stale entry reads as a known exception forever.
#
# Checked by `just test-skips`. See docs/sirens-echo-test-skips.md
# and https://forgejo.coilysiren.me/coilyco-gaming/sirens-echo/issues/291.

# Retires itself. It checks a claim capability.md no longer makes, which is a
# guard reporting that its subject is gone rather than a guard going quiet.
TestCapabilityDocIsRightThatTheBuildCarriesNoRevision

# Needs AOS_CATALOG, which CI sets nowhere. The deny list it was the only guard
# for is now covered offline in composedeny_test.go, so what stays unrun is the
# narrower question of whether roles.kdl still matches a real catalogue.
# This entry is permanent while that question needs a checkout to answer.
TestGraphPatternsNeverReachDeniedSources

# The Postgres-backed SQL, job store and turn log alike, which needs a live
# database. There is no in-process Postgres, so the choice is an env gate or no
# SQL coverage at all.
#
# These eight skip under `just test` and `test-skips` in every environment,
# including CI, because SIRENS_ECHO_TEST_JOB_STORE_DSN is deliberately not set
# job-wide. They are not unrun: the `job store SQL` CI step runs exactly this
# set against a service container, scoping the DSN to that one step so the skip
# accounting here stays true both locally and in CI.
#
# Disagree with this by pointing at a green run where the SQL never executed.
# That is the failure these entries are shaped to make visible rather than
# quiet, and the separate step is what keeps it from being one.
TestThePostgresStoreSurvivesAReopen
TestThePostgresStoreCollapsesARedeliveredSubmission
TestThePostgresStoreLeavesARefusedMoveAlone
TestThePostgresStoreFindsAJobReboundToAThread
TestThePostgresStoreReportsAMissingJob
TestThePostgresTurnLogReportsWhatAnotherRunLeft
TestThePostgresTurnLogTakesEachRecordOnce
TestThePostgresTurnLogClearsFinishedAndKeepsLive

# route.jev's latency and question-count probe (teable:coilyco-gaming/sirens-echo#8050,
# PR 1). It always measures the built question count against the real content
# taxonomy and skill roots (that half never skips - see the log line it leaves
# either way). The live half - one real request against Agent Proxy's
# /v1/systemone route, checking latency and whether the full batch is accepted
# in one call rather than needing the two-parallel-requests split - needs
# AGENT_PROXY_URL and SIRENS_ECHO_JEV_MODEL pointed at a reachable deployment,
# which no CI runner or this sandbox has. Filed as its own follow-up to run
# once against a live deployment; this entry stays until that measurement has
# a permanent home (a nightly job against a real endpoint, most likely).
TestRouteJevQuestionCountAndLatency
